# Pixel-Perfect Audit

Every section / sub-component must be audited against Figma at all three breakpoints **before** the implementation is considered finished. Do not skip this step. "Looks similar in the dev server" is not a substitute.

## When to run an audit

- Before opening a commit titled "implement <section>" or "fix <section>"
- After every user complaint about visual fidelity (always, before guessing)
- Before promoting a section into a Payload block (the block must render the same pixels as the static seed)

## What to fetch from Figma (always, in this order)

For each breakpoint variant of the section:

1. `get_metadata(fileKey, nodeId)` — the full hierarchy with x / y / width / height for every child
2. `get_design_context(fileKey, nodeId)` — the React+Tailwind reference with exact padding, gap, font, color values
3. `get_variable_defs(fileKey, nodeId)` — to confirm tokens used (typography/header/l, primary/100, …)
4. `get_screenshot(fileKey, nodeId, maxDimension: 1600+)` — for visual cross-check only, never as the primary source

Use the Figma node IDs already stored in the section's `constants.ts`. If the section doesn't have them yet — add them before auditing.

